Z||000000||Jncomutt||04-14-2001||03:42 PM||||I am still tryin to restore my recently purchased 84 2M4.  The car has been sitting for about 5 years.  The clutch didn't work when I recieved the car.  I found the slave cylinder to be frozen and all corroded inside.  I purchased a new slave cylinder and bled the system but the clutch doesn't fully engage.  <P>When you push the clutch to the floor, you can see the slave cyl rod pushing against the lever, but it will only go about 1 inch.  <P>I put the car up in the air, and started in gear and it still had all 4 gears and reverse.  The clutch does partial grab because it only grinds slightly when switching between them.  It doesn't grab enough to keep the car from moving if its pressed to the floor and started though.  <P>I've tried rebleeding the system and still haven't gotten any better movement from the slave cyl.<P>Does anyone know what could be causing this or what else I should check?  I believe this is the last thing I need to take care of before its on the road.  <P>Any help or information will be greatly appreciated.  Thanks...||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||04-15-2001||08:56 AM||||Read through the postings and you'll see a bunch of recent clutch tips. I was having a problem with mine untill I followed Archie's tips on clutch bleeding which almost cured the problem.  I also have a steel pedal which I haven't installed yet.  I may get mine power flushed as it lood a little funny when I took the bleeder valve out of the master cyl.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
